      "note": [
        "Ministry of Climate and Enterprise and Ministry of Rural Affairs and Infrastructure established in January 2023. \r\n  Ministry of Environment and Energy, Ministry of Enterprise and Ministry of Infrastructure ceased in January 2023. \r\n  Ministry of Infrastructure was established in April 2019. \r\n  Ministry for Rural Affairs ceased from 2015. \r\n  Ministry for Rural Affairs was established 2011 the in place of the former Ministry of Agriculture.",
        "Number of employees and the average monthly salary in the ministries refer to all employees at government agencies belonging to the respective ministry. The exception is the Ministry of Defence, which refers only to the number of employees and average monthly salary at the government office, government agencies belonging to the Ministry of Defence are found under the government agency group 'Defence Organization'.",
        "The target population is divided into the employed population and the salaried population. The employed population includes all employees except those on leave of absence who do not receive pay during the measurement month and employees abroad. The salaried population includes all, but not those are excluded in the employed population, who are salaried for a service of at least 40 percent and aged between 18 and 68 years. Between January 2015 and December 2022 the age limits were between 18 and 66 years. Before January 2015 the age limits were between 18 and 64 years. District Veterinarians at the Swedish Board of Agriculture and the medical officer at The Swedish Social Insurance Agency are excluded from the salaried as well.",
        "The information on the numbers of the survey is from the employed population, while the information on salaries is from the salaried population. The information on salaries for the most recent month is preliminary, the salary information for the same month one year before (and months prior to that) is definitive, while the salary information for the months in between is preliminary, plus corrections for retroactive pay."
      ],
